cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use pihm, please cite it as below, and cite the method it implements
  (Wu et al., arXiv:2504.13174).
title: "pihm: physics-informed effective Hamiltonians"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for solving differential equations as the ground state of an
  effective Hamiltonian built from their residual, in the standard form of Wu et al.
  and a banded descriptor form, verified at the level of operators, circuits and
  prepared states.
type: software
authors:
